// Endpoint posture drift: raise for review when the share of monitored endpoints
// outside their approved security posture reaches 5 percent. The advisory half
// of a pair. ENDPOINT_NONCOMPLIANT_PCT is the percentage of in-scope endpoints
// the host currently measures as out of posture.
// REGIME: all of them. Fleet posture drifts slowly and continuously; this is the
// rule that gives the drift a dated record before it becomes an incident.
// CONDITIONS: none in the rule. The host defines approved posture, decides which
// endpoints are in scope, and measures compliance. Nano cannot scan or
// quarantine an endpoint.
// INVALIDATION: remediation bringing the share back under 5 percent. No latch.
// SHAPE: 1h; posture changes over hours and days, and a faster cadence only
// repeats the same reading.
// NOT endpoint_posture_ceiling: that is the same signal at 15 percent and it
// proposes a pause. Two rules rather than one because review and hold are
// different decisions with different owners - a fleet between the two ceilings
// is drifting and needs attention, not yet a stop.
// CALIBRATED ON: policy, not data. 5 percent is a placeholder review line for a
// managed fleet; a percentage travels between fleet sizes where a count would
// not, but the line itself belongs to whoever owns the posture policy.
strategy EndpointPostureDrift {

    agent SecurityDesk

    every 1h {

        if ENDPOINT_NONCOMPLIANT_PCT >= 5 {

            observe()

        }

    }

}
